---

## TypeScript Rules

- Enable `strict: true` in tsconfig — no exceptions
- Every function must have explicit return type annotations
- Never use `any` — use `unknown` and narrow, or define proper types
- Use discriminated unions for API response states
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions and aliases
- All API responses typed via `ApiResponse<T>` generic wrapper:
  ```ts
  type ApiResponse<T> = {
    data: T;
    message: string;
    success: boolean;
  };
  ```

---

## Component Rules

- All components are functional with named exports (no default export for components)
- Props interfaces named as `ComponentNameProps` in the same file
- No inline styles — Tailwind classes only
- No hardcoded colors — use Tailwind semantic tokens
- Every component handles three states: loading, error, empty
- Use `React.memo` only when there is a demonstrated render performance need
- Server Components (RSC) by default in app/ — add `"use client"` only when required for:
  - useState / useEffect
  - Event handlers
  - Browser APIs
  - Zustand store access
- Keep client components as leaf nodes — push `"use client"` as far down the tree as possible

---

## Routing & Layout Rules

- Route groups: `(auth)`, `(tenant)`, `(saas-admin)` — never mix their layouts
- Middleware (`middleware.ts`) enforces:
  - Unauthenticated → redirect to `/login`
  - `saas_admin` role → can only access `/saas/*`
  - `teacher` role → blocked from fees, expenses, payroll, settings routes
  - Active session required for all tenant routes
- Dynamic segments: `[id]` for resource detail pages
- Each route segment has its own `loading.tsx` and `error.tsx`

---

## Auth & Permissions

### Roles (exactly these four, no others)
```ts
type Role = 'saas_admin' | 'owner' | 'admin' | 'teacher';
```

### Permission Matrix
```ts
// lib/permissions.ts
const PERMISSIONS = {
  students: { view: ['owner','admin','teacher'], manage: ['owner','admin'] },
  admissions: { manage: ['owner','admin'] },
  attendance: { view: ['owner','admin','teacher'], manage: ['owner','admin','teacher'] },
  fees: { view: ['owner','admin'], manage: ['owner','admin'] },
  staff: { view: ['owner','admin'], manage: ['owner'] },
  payroll: { view: ['owner'], manage: ['owner'] },
  expenses: { view: ['owner','admin'], manage: ['owner','admin'] },
  exams: { view: ['owner','admin','teacher'], manage: ['owner','admin'] },
  reports: { view: ['owner','admin'] },
  analytics: { view: ['owner','admin'] },
  settings: { manage: ['owner'] },
  saas_dashboard: { view: ['saas_admin'] },
} as const;
```

- `usePermissions()` hook checks current user role against permission matrix
- Sidebar nav items rendered conditionally based on permissions
- Route-level guard in middleware is the source of truth — component-level is secondary

---

## Data Fetching Patterns

```ts
// All server data via TanStack Query hooks in /hooks/
// Example pattern:
export function useStudents(filters: StudentFilters) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['students', filters],
    queryFn: () => api.get<PaginatedResponse<Student>>('/students', { params: filters }),
    staleTime: 30_000,
  });
}

// Mutations always invalidate relevant query keys on success
// Always handle onError with toast notification
```

- Optimistic updates for attendance toggling (high-frequency action)
- No direct fetch() calls — always go through the Axios instance in `lib/api.ts`
- `lib/api.ts` Axios instance attaches Authorization header from Zustand auth store
- 401 response → clear auth store → redirect to login

---

## Form Rules

```ts
// All forms: React Hook Form + Zod
// Schema defined in lib/validators/, imported in form component
// Submit button disabled while submitting
// Field errors shown inline below input
// No alert() or console.log in production paths
```

- Admission form is multi-step (3 steps): Student Info → Guardian Info → Academic & Fee Info
- Fee collection form is single-screen with student search at top
- All forms show a loading spinner on the submit button during mutation

---

## UI Patterns & Design System

### Color Palette (Tailwind config extension)
```js
// Primary: Indigo — professional, trustworthy
// Accent: Emerald — success states, active items  
// Destructive: Rose — errors, deletions
// Neutral: Slate — text, borders, backgrounds
colors: {
  primary: { DEFAULT: '#4F46E5', ... },   // indigo-600
  success: { DEFAULT: '#10B981', ... },   // emerald-500
  warning: { DEFAULT: '#F59E0B', ... },   // amber-500
  danger:  { DEFAULT: '#F43F5E', ... },   // rose-500
}
```

### Sidebar
- Width: 240px (expanded), 64px (collapsed icon-only)
- Collapsible on mobile → Sheet drawer
- Active route: `bg-primary/10 text-primary font-medium`
- Grouped nav sections with subtle section labels
- School name + logo at top of sidebar
- User avatar + name at bottom of sidebar

### Metric Cards (Dashboard)
- White background, 1px border, subtle shadow
- Large number (text-3xl font-bold)
- Label below in text-sm text-muted-foreground
- Trend indicator (up/down arrow + percentage) where applicable
- Icon in top-right corner in muted color

### Tables (DataTable)
- Built on TanStack Table v8 via reusable `<DataTable>` component
- Pagination: 25 rows default
- Column header click = sort
- Filter bar above table (search input + dropdowns)
- Row actions in last column: View, Edit, Delete (icon buttons)
- Empty state: illustration + message + primary CTA

### Status Badges
```ts
// Student status
Active → green badge
Inactive → gray badge
Graduated → blue badge
Withdrawn → orange badge

// Fee/Payroll status
Paid → green
Unpaid → red
Partial → yellow

// Attendance
Present → green dot
Absent → red dot
```

### Modals and Drawers
- Create/Edit forms → Sheet (side drawer, 480px wide)
- Destructive confirmations → Dialog (centered modal)
- Quick views → Dialog
- Never open a new page for CRUD — use Sheet/Dialog

### Toast Notifications (Sonner)
```ts
toast.success('Fee collected successfully')
toast.error('Failed to save. Please try again.')
// Keep messages short, specific, and action-confirming
```

---

## Currency & Locale

```ts
// lib/utils.ts
export function formatCurrency(amount: number): string {
  return `Rs. ${amount.toLocaleString('en-PK')}`;
}
// Output: Rs. 8,000 / Rs. 2,450,000
// Never abbreviate: not "8K", not "$"
```

---

## Pakistani Context Rules

- Student ID format: `ADM-2026-0001`
- Receipt number format: `#REC-000421`
- Phone numbers: Pakistani format (03XX-XXXXXXX)
- CNIC: XXXXX-XXXXXXX-X format with mask
- Academic session names: `2025-26`, `2026-27`
- Fee months: Full month + year (August 2026, not Aug-26)
- All dates: DD/MM/YYYY display format, ISO 8601 storage
- WhatsApp phone numbers default to +92 country code

---

## Naming Conventions

- Files: `PascalCase` for components, `camelCase` for hooks/utils/types
- Components: PascalCase (`StudentTable`, `FeeCollectionForm`)
- Hooks: `useCamelCase` (`useStudents`, `usePermissions`)
- Zustand stores: `camelCaseStore` (`authStore`, `uiStore`)
- API routes (when building): kebab-case (`/api/fee-collection`)
- DB field references in types: `snake_case` to match backend (`school_id`, `student_id`)
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`

---

## Performance Rules

- All images use Next.js `<Image>` component — no `<img>` tags
- Dynamic imports for heavy components (PDF viewer, charts on analytics page)
- Tables never render more than 25 rows without pagination
- Attendance sheet uses virtualization if student list > 50
- No `useEffect` for data fetching — always TanStack Query

---

## Code Quality Rules

- No commented-out code in commits
- No TODO comments without a GitHub issue reference
- No console.log in components — use proper error boundaries
- Every API call wrapped in try/catch or TanStack Query error handling
- No hardcoded strings for UI labels — define in a constants file or inline clearly
- Zod schema is the single source of truth for form validation AND TypeScript type inference

---

## What NOT To Build

- No student/parent login portal (explicitly out of scope)
- No online classes, homework, library, hostel, or transport modules
- No complex accounting (no double-entry, no tax calculations)
- No AI features
- No biometric integrations
- Do not add tabs, sections, or form fields not described in the spec
- Do not build a page router version — App Router only

---

## File Generation Order (For Cursor Completions)

When generating new features, always follow this order:
1. Types (`types/*.types.ts`)
2. Zod schema (`lib/validators/*.schema.ts`)
3. API hook (`hooks/use*.ts`)
4. Component(s) (`components/feature/`)
5. Page (`app/(tenant)/feature/page.tsx`)

---

## Accessibility Baseline

- All interactive elements have `aria-label` or visible label
- Focus rings visible (never `outline-none` without a substitute)
- Color is never the only indicator of state (always pair with text or icon)
- Form fields always have associated `<label>` elements
- Keyboard navigable sidebar
